      "writtenOn": "2025-02-10T09:46:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not for this CL, but... now that we have fuzzy-matching, it\u0027s not really correct for this to be indexed by the int tethering type any more. With fuzzy-matching, the invariant should be this can be a Set, and requests can be admitted to the Set only if they do not fuzzy-match an existing request in the set.\n\nSo maybe we can somewhat unify the old and the new codepaths by making this a Set, and making the fuzzy-matching, on previous releases, only check the type.\n\nThen when a caller wants to start tethering, we would check if a fuzzy-matching request is already in the Set, and if it is, on new releases send DUPLICATE_REQUEST, and on older releases run the legacy \"stop the existing request and start the new request\" code.",
      "range": {
